WEBVTT

00:04:59.185 --> 00:05:00.740
in your field or your workplace.

00:05:00.764 --> 00:05:03.785
Or maybe you've been humming along
feeling good about your work,

00:05:03.809 --> 00:05:05.040
until one day you noticed

00:05:05.064 --> 00:05:07.901
your skills don't seem quite
as sharp as they used to.

00:05:08.314 --> 00:05:12.718
In 2019, Arthur wrote a major story
about this phenomenon in "The Atlantic."

00:05:12.742 --> 00:05:13.926
The headline was

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:16.100
"Your Professional Decline Is Coming

00:05:16.124 --> 00:05:18.210
(Much) Sooner Than You Think."

00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:22.052
As in, long before you even start
to see retirement on the horizon.

00:05:22.076 --> 00:05:24.381
AB: I mean the number one myth
is that, you know,

00:05:24.405 --> 00:05:26.151
particularly in certain professions,

00:05:26.175 --> 00:05:27.980
like, let's just say yours and mine,

00:05:28.004 --> 00:05:30.477
which is coming up
with big ideas and sharing them,